{% set reviewEmail = "mailto:dan@sensecall.co.uk?subject=Product%20and%20service%20review" %}

{% from "macros/cta-button.njk" import ctaButton %}

<section aria-labelledby="page-title" class="py-8 lg:py-12">
    <div class="page-hero">
        <div class="page-hero__intro">
            <h1 id="page-title" class="heading-l">Independent product and service reviews</h1>
            <p class="body-l">
                A clear outside view of what is working, what is getting in the way and what to do next.
            </p>
        </div>
        <figure class="page-hero__image">
            <img src="/assets/images/product-service-review-480.webp"
                 srcset="/assets/images/product-service-review-480.webp 480w,
                         /assets/images/product-service-review-1024.webp 1024w"
                 sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 40vw, min(28rem, calc(100vw - 2rem))"
                 alt="Papers on a desk showing a service map, a screen layout, notes and a notebook, with a pen and a cup of coffee"
                 width="1024"
                 height="696"
                 fetchpriority="high"
                 decoding="async"
                 class="h-auto w-full rounded-lg">
        </figure>
        <div class="page-hero__body">
            <p class="body-m">
                When you are close to a product or service, it can be difficult to see which problems matter most. You may have concerns about the experience, a proposed direction or the way a programme is approaching delivery, but need someone experienced to examine the evidence and give you a considered view.
            </p>
            <p class="body-m">
                I carry out focused reviews of digital products, services and work in progress. I bring together service design, UX and product thinking to help your team make its next decisions.
            </p>
            <p class="body-m mt-6">{{ ctaButton(reviewEmail, "Discuss a review") }}</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="what-i-can-review" class="panel">
    <h2 id="what-i-can-review" class="heading-m mt-0">What I can review</h2>
    {% set situations = [
        {
            title: "An existing product or service",
            description: "Where are people struggling? Which problems sit in the interface, and which come from the wider service around it?"
        },
        {
            title: "A proposed change or prototype",
            description: "Does the approach address the problem? What assumptions need testing before the team builds further?"
        },
        {
            title: "A legacy replacement",
            description: "Will the new service let people complete the work they need to do, or are important needs and dependencies being missed?"
        },
        {
            title: "The direction of a programme",
            description: "Do the research, priorities and planned work support the outcomes the programme is trying to achieve?"
        }
    ] %}
    <ul class="mt-6 grid list-none grid-cols-1 gap-8 p-0 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-x-12 md:gap-y-8" role="list">
        {% for item in situations %}
            <li class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-4 dark:border-gray-700">
                <h3 class="heading-xs mt-0">{{ item.title }}</h3>
                <p class="body-m mb-0">{{ item.description }}</p>
            </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="what-you-receive" class="py-8 md:py-10 lg:py-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 id="what-you-receive" class="heading-m">What you receive</h2>
        <p class="body-m">
            We agree the question and scope before I start. I then review the relevant product or service, look at the evidence you already have and speak with key people where that will help.
        </p>
        <p class="body-m">You receive a concise written assessment setting out:</p>
        <ul class="body-m list-disc pl-5">
            <li>what appears to be working</li>
            <li>the most important problems and risks</li>
            <li>where the evidence is strong or still missing</li>
            <li>practical recommendations, in priority order</li>
            <li>what I suggest the team does next</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="body-m">
            I'll talk the findings through with you, so the people making decisions can question them and work out how to respond. The scope and fee are agreed upfront.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="about-me" class="py-8 md:py-10 lg:py-12">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 id="about-me" class="heading-m">About me</h2>
        <p class="body-m">
            I'm Dan Sensecall. My work spans service design, interaction design, research and prototyping, with extensive experience of complex public-sector services and digital products.
        </p>
        <p class="body-m">
            I'm used to looking beyond individual screens to understand the tasks people need to complete, the teams involved and the systems a service depends on. You can see examples in my <a href="/projects/" class="text-link">project case studies</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="request-review" class="pb-8 md:pb-10 lg:pb-12 xl:pb-14">
    <div class="cta-card max-w-3xl">
        <h2 id="request-review" class="heading-m mt-0">Tell me what you would like reviewed</h2>
        <p class="body-m">
            You do not need to know exactly what the answer should look like. Tell me what concerns you, what you have already learned and what decision the review needs to inform. I'll suggest a useful scope and let you know if a review is the right way to help.
        </p>
        <p class="body-m mt-6">{{ ctaButton(reviewEmail, "Email me about a review") }}</p>
    </div>
</section>
